# Every binary package of decision 0019's package table. Each owns one directory,
# /usr/lib/photo-wall/<name>/ (<name> is the package name without `photo-wall-`), and gets its
# own content-derived version, 0+<12 hex> (debian/content-versions). A sibling is named at its
# exact version as `<sibling> (= ${pw-version:<sibling>})`. Third-party Depends are added by the
# slice that fills the package, and only the computed import check may change them after.
#
# appliance/display_host is built by debhelper's Meson build system (debian/rules). Its
# Build-Depends end with the runtime Depends that no build tool needs (python3-cairo, weston,
# python3-pydantic): debian/graphics-abi binds the resolved version of every third-party package
# the display and the frame client Depend on, and the import check (scripts/import_check.py)
# resolves every third-party import to its owner, so the build root holds each of them.
# python3-cffi-backend is an OS dependency of trixie's python3-pywayland (0.4.18-4), which
# imports it without declaring it: the build root needs it to generate the overlay's bindings,
# and the base gets it from rpi-image-gen (appliance/rpi_image_gen/layer/photo-wall-device.yaml),
# never from a Photo Wall package (R4).

Package: photo-wall-common
Architecture: all
Depends: python3,
 python3-nats,
 python3-pydantic,
 ${misc:Depends}
Description: Photo Wall wire contracts and Node API
 The contracts and nodeapi import roots every Node program shares.

Package: photo-wall-uplink
Architecture: all
Depends: python3,
 photo-wall-common (= ${pw-version:photo-wall-common}),
 ${misc:Depends}
Description: Photo Wall uplink: locating and trusting Central
 The stdlib-only uplink import root, shared by stage 1 and the Node's programs.

Package: photo-wall-node-kernel
